# OpenWiki maintenance (default)

Agent-oriented docs live in `openwiki/` (OKF). Treat them as a first-class deliverable for this repo.

## Read

- For repo layout, modules, actions, runtime paths, automation, or invariants: start at `openwiki/index.md`, then the linked concept page — do not dump the whole wiki into context.
- Prefer the wiki over blind grepping; then open the named source file.

## Update (default, not optional)

**Do not wait for the user to say “update wiki” / “document this”.** Self-documentation is part of finishing any material change (same bar as a green build).

When you **add, remove, rename, or materially change** any of the following, update the matching wiki pages in the **same change** (before finishing):

- Top-level folders / surfaces → `openwiki/index.md` + `overview.md`
- `src/*` modules or MCP surface → `openwiki/modules/`
- Tools, Telegram commands, Pi slash, or `teleg` CLI → `openwiki/actions/`
- Config / DB / lock / relay paths → `openwiki/runtime/`
- Polling / routing / relay flow → `openwiki/architecture.md`
- Hard invariants / bugs → `openwiki/gotchas.md`
- Install / deploy → `openwiki/automation.md`
- Plan status → `openwiki/plans/`

Also append a short entry to `openwiki/log.md` for non-trivial wiki edits.

## Format

- Concept pages: YAML front matter with `type`, `title`, `description`, `tags`
- Reserved: nested `index.md` (no concept front matter) and `log.md`
- Document **why / invariants**, not a code dump; never invent paths that are not on disk
- Keep `openwiki/INSTRUCTIONS.md` as the human brief; do not rewrite it unless asked

## Do not skip

Finishing a structural or user-visible feature/API/tool change without an OpenWiki update is incomplete work in this repo — whether or not the user mentioned docs.
